What is an Exception?
Definition

An Exception is any error that disturbs the normal flow of instructions during the execution of a program.

Simple Explanation

Normally a program executes step by step:

step1-->step2-->step3

If an error occurs:
step1-->step2-->error

The interruption is called an Exception.
-------------------------------------------
Deviation

An exception can also be viewed as a deviation from the expected business output.
xample

Expected Output:
Invoice Amount = ₹5000

Actual Output:
Blank Value

This deviation creates an exception.
---------------------------------------------------------
General Exceptions

Some common exceptions are:

Time Exception
I/O Exception
User Exception
Class Exception
